---
import { links } from "../site.ts";

/**
 * Every figure here is from BENCHMARKS.md, measured against the compiled SBF binary with
 * Mollusk on a Small market at 2 bps. Nothing is estimated and nothing is rounded in this
 * direction or that. If the table there changes, this changes.
 */
const rows = [
  { what: "Claim a seat", cu: 227, note: "Once per wallet, per market" },
  { what: "Post-only, empty book", cu: 574, note: "The cheapest thing a maker does" },
  { what: "Cancel one order", cu: 844, note: "" },
  { what: "Market order, one level", cu: 1_500, note: "" },
  { what: "Batch: 4 cancels, 4 places", cu: 3_251, note: "An entire two-sided ladder" },
  { what: "Market order, four levels", cu: 4_480, note: "About 1,000 CU per level after the first" },
  { what: "Swap, no seat", cu: 6_417, note: "Both legs through the token program" },
];

const budget = 1_400_000;
---

<section class="band" id="compute">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="band-head">
      <p class="eyebrow reveal">Measured, not estimated</p>
      <h2 class="reveal" style="--delay:60ms">
        Compute is the constraint. Here is ours.
      </h2>
      <p class="lede reveal" style="--delay:120ms">
        Compute decides how deep a taker can sweep, how many quotes a maker can refresh at
        once, and whether an aggregator's route through you fits its budget at all. Every
        number below comes from executing the compiled binary — not from a model of it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      <ul class="table reveal">
        {
          rows.map((row) => (
            <li class="row">
              <span class="what">
                {row.what}
                {row.note && <em>{row.note}</em>}
              </span>
              <span class="cu num">{row.cu.toLocaleString("en-US")}</span>
              <span class="bar" style={`--fill:${(row.cu / 7000) * 100}%`} />
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <aside class="notes">
        <div class="note reveal" style="--delay:80ms">
          <p class="k num data">32%</p>
          <p>
            cheaper to batch four cancels and four places than to send them as eight
            instructions — 4,639 CU against 6,820, measured on one fixture. One transaction
            instead of eight matters more: eight is eight signatures and eight chances to
            land out of order.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="note reveal" style="--delay:160ms">
          <p class="k num data">0.2%</p>
          <p>
            of a {budget.toLocaleString("en-US")} CU transaction is what a full ladder
            refresh costs. The binding constraint on a sweep is the match limit the caller
            sets, not the budget.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="note reveal" style="--delay:240ms">
          <p class="k num">log n</p>
          <p>
            is how seat lookup scales — 782 CU at two seats, 863 at thirty. A scan would tax
            a market for succeeding, and since seats are cheap and permissionless it would
            be a griefing vector too. A test asserts the shape.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <!-- The part most venues leave out. A number is only worth something if the method
         behind it can be pointed at whatever you want to compare against. -->
    <p class="method reveal">
      No comparison column, deliberately: we have not measured other venues, and filling it
      in with figures that look authoritative would be worse than leaving it empty. The
      method is published and needs no cooperation from anyone — <code>simulateTransaction</code>
      requires no signature that spends anything, so the same procedure runs against any
      program on the chain, including this one.
      <a href={links.benchmarks} rel="noopener">Read the method →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .band {
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--ink-2) 0%, var(--dawn-1) 100%);
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .table {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgb(4 5 10 / 0.4);
  }

  .row {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .what {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .what em {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-3);
  }

  .cu {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--data);
  }

  /* The bar grows as its row arrives, so the column reads as a comparison rather than as
     a list of numbers. Width is set from the datum, not animated to an arbitrary place. */
  .bar {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    height: 2px;
    width: var(--fill);
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(200 247 81 / 0.05), rgb(200 247 81 / 0.5));
    transform-origin: left;
    scale: 0 1;
    transition: scale 1.1s var(--ease);
    transition-delay: 0.15s;
  }

  .table.in .bar {
    scale: 1 1;
  }

  .notes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--line);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .note {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
    background: rgb(4 5 10 / 0.45);
  }

  .note p:last-child {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .k {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .method {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--dawn-3);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 74ch;
  }

  .method code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .method a {
    color: var(--dawn-4);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .method a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
